#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
NORA Phase 2.6
==============
Production-oriented offline NLP/ML pipeline for:
  * corpus-derived noise reduction
  * near-duplicate/template control
  * robust latent text representation
  * UMAP + HDBSCAN model selection and stability analysis
  * recursive refinement of oversized/heterogeneous clusters
  * privacy-safe audited outputs
  * persisted model artifacts and inference on unseen data

Design principles
-----------------
1. No manually curated NORA intent/noise keyword lists.
2. Development/test isolation before every learned transformation.
3. Noise is learned statistically from development data only.
4. Learned noise is removed from BOTH word and character model channels,
   while redacted source text is retained intact for review.
5. Approximate nearest-neighbour duplicate detection is used at scale.
6. Cluster selection uses multiple intrinsic/stability criteria rather than
   a single silhouette score.
7. Noise-policy choice is development-only and data-driven; no feature branch is privileged by assumption.
8. Borderline outlier recovery is conservative, cluster-specific, persisted, and identical in train/test/inference.
9. Interpretability uses phrase-aware NPMI on one fixed redacted development reference corpus.
10. Structural safety, semantic regression protection, and SME business acceptance are separate decisions.
11. Raw/unredacted text and raw business identifiers are never exported.
12. Fitted artifacts are persisted for reproducible inference.

This is an offline architecture. It does not download pretrained models or call
external APIs/LLMs.
"""

